  "notes": "{挽|ひ}く specifically means to grind food items. It shares the reading ひく with ⟦{引|ひ}く→引く：01978_hiku⟧ (to pull) and ⟦{弾|ひ}く→弾く：02444_hiku⟧ (to play an instrument), but these are different words with different kanji.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: ⟦{他動詞|たどうし}→他動詞：10418_tadoushi⟧ (transitive)\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- ⟦コーヒー→コーヒー：00789_koohii⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{挽|ひ}く: to grind coffee\n- ⟦{豆|まめ}→豆：03738_mame⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{挽|ひ}く: to grind beans\n- ⟦{肉|にく}→肉：02240_niku⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{挽|ひ}く: to mince meat\n- コショウ⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{挽|ひ}く: to grind pepper\n- {挽|ひ}き{肉|にく}: ground meat, minced meat\n- ⟦{挽|ひ}きたて→挽きたて：21367_hikitate⟧: freshly ground\n- {粗挽|あらび}き: coarsely ground\n\nNOTE: The compound {挽|ひ}き{肉|にく} (ground meat) is one of the most common words using this kanji. It appears on supermarket labels throughout Japan.",
